>Fiedler</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Veit</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Stamnes</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Rothman</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bimodal interaction of coatomer with the p24 family of putative cargo receptors</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1996</year><volume>273</volume><fpage>1396</fpage><lpage>1399</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8703076</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gruenberg</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Griffiths</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Howell</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characterization of the early endosome and putative endocytic carrier vesicles in vivo and with an assay of vesicle fusion in vitro</article-title><source>J Cell Biol</source><year>1989</year><volume>108</volume><fpage>1301</fpage><lpage>1317</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2538480</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gruenberg</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Maxfield</surname><given-names>FR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Membrane transport in the endocytic pathway</article-title><source>Curr Opin Cell Biol</source><year>1995</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>552</fpage><lpage>563</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7495576</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guo</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Vasile</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Krieger</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Disruptions in Golgi structure and membrane traffic in a conditional lethal mammalian cell mutant are corrected by &#x003b5;-COP</article-title><source>J Cell Biol</source><year>1994</year><volume>125</volume><fpage>1213</fpage><lpage>1224</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8207054</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guo</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Penman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Trigatti</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Krieger</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A single point mutation in &#x003b5;-COP results in temperature-sensitive, lethal defects in membrane transport in a Chinese hamster ovary cell mutant</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1996</year><volume>271</volume><fpage>11191</fpage><lpage>11196</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8626666</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Harter</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Mellman</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transport of the lysosomal membrane glycoprotein lgp120 (lgp-A) to lysosomes does not require appearance on the plasma membrane</article-title><source>J Cell Biol</source><year>1992</year><volume>117</volume><fpage>311</fpage><lpage>325</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1560028</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Helms</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Rothman</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inhibition by brefeldin A of a Golgi membrane enzyme that catalyses exchange of guanine nucleotide bound to ARF</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1992</year><volume>360</volume><fpage>352</fp